---
// Traduction de src/pages/cgu.astro, qui seule fait foi : toute modification de l'une
// se reporte sur l'autre dans le même commit (scripts/check-legal-parity.mjs).
import { localePath } from '../../i18n';
import ContentLayout from '../../layouts/content-layout.astro';
---

<ContentLayout
    title="Terms of use - TryCast"
    description="Terms of use of TryCast, the free rugby predictions game to play with your mates."
    heading="Terms of use"
    route="terms">
    <h2>1. Purpose</h2>
    <p>
        These terms of use (the “Terms”) govern the use of the TryCast mobile app and the
        trycast.fr website (together, the “Service”). TryCast is a <strong>free</strong> rugby
        predictions game to play with friends: you predict the results of matches, score points
        and compare yourself with the people close to you on leaderboards.
    </p>
    <p>
        By creating an account or using the Service, you accept these Terms. If you disagree with
        any of them, do not use the Service.
    </p>

    <h2>2. A free game, with no real money</h2>
    <p>
        TryCast is <strong>not a real-money betting service</strong>: no stakes, no winnings in cash
        or in kind, no in-app purchases. Points and leaderboards have no monetary value and can be
        neither exchanged nor cashed in. The odds displayed are used solely to calculate the
        game's points and constitute neither an incentive nor an offer to bet.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Account and access</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            Creating an account requires a valid email address and a username. You are
            responsible for keeping your login details confidential.
        </li>
        <li>
            The Service is reserved for people aged 16 or over. If you are under 18, make sure you
            have the consent of a parent or guardian.
        </li>
        <li>
            You can delete your account at any time from the app's settings; deletion is
            permanent.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Rules of use</h2>
    <p>By using the Service, you agree to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>choose a username and a league name that are neither offensive nor misleading;</li>
        <li>not attempt to rig the leaderboards, automate access to the Service or get around its
            protections;</li>
        <li>not use the Service for commercial or unlawful purposes.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        In the event of a breach, the publisher may suspend or delete the account concerned, after
        notice where possible.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Content and competitions</h2>
    <p>
        Fixtures, results and odds come from third-party data providers and are provided for
        information only; errors or delays may occur. TryCast is an independent project, <strong>not
        affiliated</strong> with the competitions, unions, clubs or brands mentioned in the app.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Availability and liability</h2>
    <p>
        TryCast is a project run by an independent developer, provided “as is” with no guarantee of
        continuous availability. The publisher does everything it can to provide a reliable
        service, but cannot be held liable for interruptions, loss of game data or indirect damage
        arising from the use of the Service, to the extent permitted by law.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
        The TryCast brand, logo, interface and original content of the Service are protected. Any
        unauthorised reproduction or use is prohibited.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Personal data</h2>
    <p>
        How your data is processed is described in the <a href={localePath('privacy', 'en')}>privacy
        policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Changes to these Terms</h2>
    <p>
        These Terms may change, particularly when new features launch. In the event of a
        substantial change, you will be informed in the app or by email; continuing to use the
        Service constitutes acceptance.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
        These Terms are governed by French law. Any dispute falls under the jurisdiction of the
        competent French courts, subject to mandatory consumer protection rules.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Contact</h2>
    <p>
        For any question: <a href="mailto:contact@trycast.fr">contact@trycast.fr</a>.
    </p>
</ContentLayout>
